Subject: [PATCH 09/20] fix(forms): remove the dead homepage newsletter form,
 rewire the FAQ inquiry form to Formspree
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 14 batch B5 (audit 2026-09-01, Phase 12 CV-1). Two WordPress-era
Kadence forms still posted to action="" with the hidden WP admin-ajax
router field (kb_process_ajax_submit), which does not exist on the static
host — both have been dead since the migration and told no-JS users to
'enable JavaScript'.
- Homepage 'Subscribe to our newsletter' row: removed at render time
  (render-snapshot.ts). There is no newsletter programme to point it at;
  a visibly broken form is worse than none. Guarded on the newsletter
  wording so no other form is touched.
- /faq/ 'Can't find an answer?' form: rewired to the shared Formspree inbox
  with the same field mapping, honeypot rename and a11y/attribution
  hardening as /contact/ (helpers extracted from enhancePrimaryContactPage).
- Both Kadence forms drop the WP-only <noscript> 'enable JavaScript'
  warning (and its style hiding the submit button) — the native POST works
  without JavaScript now.
FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT is exported once and reused.
